SGX530: FastBlur's 4-tap average without lowp overflow

texture2D() on a lowp sampler returns lowp, and the N9's SGX530 keeps lowp in [-2, 2]: the
sum of four taps clamped at 2 before the * 0.25, so opaque pixels came out with alpha 0.5
(and green and blue capped at 0.5 too). FastBlur, FastGlow, FastInnerShadow and
FastMaskedBlur blurred too light, see-through. Each tap is scaled before the sum.

--- a/src/effects/shaders/fastblur_internal.frag
+++ b/src/effects/shaders/fastblur_internal.frag
@@ -6,9 +6,9 @@
 varying highp vec2 qt_TexCoord3;
 
 void main() {
-    highp vec4 sourceColor = (texture2D(source, qt_TexCoord0) +
-    texture2D(source, qt_TexCoord1) +
-    texture2D(source, qt_TexCoord2) +
-    texture2D(source, qt_TexCoord3)) * 0.25;
+    highp vec4 sourceColor = texture2D(source, qt_TexCoord0) * 0.25 +
+    texture2D(source, qt_TexCoord1) * 0.25 +
+    texture2D(source, qt_TexCoord2) * 0.25 +
+    texture2D(source, qt_TexCoord3) * 0.25;
     gl_FragColor = sourceColor * qt_Opacity;
 }
